
! This file defines a Left-handed Porro pair of prisms for image inversion.
! (Lefthanded as in a pair of binoculars)

! The prisms have a nominal aperture of 20mm and are drawn in the orientation
! usually found in a pair of binoculars. They are spaced 1 mm apart.
  
! The prism coordinates are defined with the optical axis (z-axis) passing
! through the centre of the normal input face. The optical axis is thefore
! displaced at the prism exit by -28.2843 in the x-direction

!------------!

! Define vertices

! Prism 1

V 1 0.0 -14.14213562 0.0
V 2 -14.14213562 0.0 0.0
V 3 14.14213562 28.28427125 0.0
V 4 28.28427125 14.14213562 0.0
V 5 14.14213562 0.0 20.0
V 6 0.0 14.14213562 20.0

! Prism 2

V 7 0.0 14.14213562 -1.0
V 8 14.14213562 28.28427125 -1.0
V 9 42.42640687 0.0 -1.0
V 10 28.28427125 -14.14213562 -1.0
V 11 14.14213562 0.0 -21.0
V 12 28.28427125 14.14213562 -21.0

!Define prisms

! Prism 1

! Input/output face (hypotenuse)

R 1 2 3 4 0 0

! Rear faces (TIR usually -- hence isreflective = 0 - set to 1 if silvered)

R 1 2 6 5 0 0
R 3 4 5 6 0 0

! Top face (ground surface therefore isreflective = -1)

T 2 6 3 -1 0

! Bottom face ( - ditto - )

T 1 5 4 -1 0

! End of prism 1


!------------!

! Prism 2


! Input/output face (hypotenuse)

R 7 8 9 10 0 0

! Rear faces (TIR usually -- hence isreflective = 0 - set to 1 if silvered)

R 7 8 12 11 0 0
R 9 10 11 12 0 0

! Top face (ground surface therefore isreflective = -1)

T 8 12 9 -1 0

! Bottom face ( - ditto - )

T 7 11 10 -1 0

! End of prism 2

!---End of file---!